# Track the canonical machine configs; ignore any extras the user adds locally.
*
!.gitignore
!default.yaml
!gpu_example.yaml
# rci*.yaml is a shared CTU cluster, not a personal box. Three shapes, because
# one file cannot describe both node types or both GPU counts: rci.yaml is the
# AMD CPU node (a[01-16], no GPU), rci_gpu.yaml one A100 on the AMD GPU node
# (g[01-12]), rci_gpu2.yaml two.
#
# rci_gpu2.yaml is listed because this pattern already lost it once: the
# 2-card config was validated on hardware in B4 (jobs 11325473/11325609) and
# then silently ignored as a "local extra", so the repo kept only the 1-card
# config that fits a single run. Add new shared cluster configs here.
!rci.yaml
!rci_gpu.yaml
!rci_gpu2.yaml
!README.md
